You are expanding a **reference** entry from a seed description into
its full form. A ref holds implementation-detail content the chain
needs to consult but didn't itself generate — a DSL spec, a runbook,
a design memo, an implementation guide. Downstream tiers that attach
this ref read your `<title>` and `<body>` as the source document;
your job is to expand the seed faithfully, not to invent facts the
seed doesn't support.

# Input

Seed description: {{ seed }}

# Output format

Emit a single `<reference>` block:

    <reference>
      <title>...</title>
      <body>...</body>
      <see-also>
        <ref target="ref_..."/>        <!-- optional, repeated -->
      </see-also>
    </reference>

# Rules

* `<title>` is a short, specific handle for this reference — specific
  enough that an agent deciding whether to attach it can tell what it
  covers without opening the body.
* `<body>` is the expanded content. Stay faithful to the seed: supply
  structure, organization, and connective prose, but do not assert
  facts, decisions, or specifics the seed didn't give you. Where the
  seed is silent on a detail, write generic guidance rather than a
  fabricated specific.
* `<see-also>` is optional — include a `<ref target="ref_..."/>` only
  when the seed itself names another reference by id; do not invent
  target ids.
* Do not include commentary outside the `<reference>` block.
{% comment %}
  Guard on `.size > 0`, never on bare `feedback` (ORC-134). Liquid
  counts an empty list as truthy — only nil and false are falsy — so a
  bare truthiness guard opens this section on every render for any
  caller that passes an empty list instead of omitting the variable.
  Catapult.Generation.ContextAssembly omits it today, and this guard is
  what stops that promise from being the only thing holding the line.
  A filter pipe (size via `|`) is not an option: a pipe inside a
  conditional needs Solid.parse/2's filters_in_conditional_tags, and
  the caller uses Solid.parse/1. `.size` is a property access, so it
  parses as-is.
{% endcomment %}
